# Repository Standards

<!-- merged from: atlas/13-atlas-repository-standards -->

- Keep the standard Node / Python service layout (see `core/technology-stack.mdc` per zone).
- Use sequential port ranges per zone (see `27-local-dev-ports.mdc` in Atlas for local dev port map).
- Each repo needs a clear `README.md` with purpose, setup steps, and design-control links.
- Use shared packages in `packages/` instead of duplicating code across services or experiences.
- Docker images use multi-stage builds and must be deployable to Azure Container Apps.
- Keep frontend / API / worker separation explicit in both repo structure and deployment boundaries.
